    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d572">

                <pb facs="0698" n="692" sameAs="frus:frus1942v03/pg692"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.51/2932: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Thurston</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kuibyshev</hi> (<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Moscow</hi>)</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-02-21T12:00:00+03:00">February 21,
                        1942—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 5:40 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>153. The Moscow press of February 19 published without comment a Tass<anchor
                        n="63" xml:id="d572-f1"/> despatch from Washington dated February 17 and
                    reporting <pb facs="0699" n="693" xml:id="pg693"/> the remarks made by the
                    President at a press conference concerning the extension of a further loan to
                    the Soviet Union. The President is quoted as having stated that a second loan is
                    necessary in order to ensure an uninterrupted flow of war materials to Russia,
                    insomuch as the first loan has been entirely allocated; that delivery of war
                    materials from the United States to the Soviet Union lagged behind plan in
                    December and January but will be on schedule by the first of March; and that
                    after March 1 the Soviet Union will receive regularly many materials in
                    accordance with the first agreement based upon the Lease-Lend across the
                    Atlantic.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Thurston</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
